{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/552079-forsaken-leans-on-the-social-manuevering-system-a-lot-more-than-requiem-doesn-t-it","id":552079,"title":"Forsaken leans on the Social Manuevering system a lot more than Requiem, doesn't it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-12T13:26:15-07:00","id":552079,"title":"Forsaken leans on the Social Manuevering system a lot more than Requiem, doesn't it?","content":"I'm continuing my read-through of Forsaken, and it seems they've done a lot more to integrate the Social Maneuvering system into the heart of the game than Requiem did. Requiem had some pieces (mostly Merits) that depended on it pretty heavily, but Werewolf seems to be much more the case. It also seems to expect PCs will more often have Social Maneuvering used against them.<br /> <br /> Anyone have an experiences/advice with social maneuvering in play they want to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:10:57-07:00","id":552162,"title":"","content":"In my experience, Social Maneuvering works best when the ST is generous with Impressions and the players are not afraid to use Soft Leverage and/or Force Doors. Also, my house rule for Social Maneuvering against PCs is that once all their Doors have been opened, they gain the Leveraged Condition tagged to the person who opened them. I find it works pretty well because it doesn't force players to do whatever an NPC wants, but it gives them a bit of an incentive to agree to their requests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:20:26-07:00","id":552323,"title":"","content":"Ehh... not really. Werewolf has a number of Gifts that relate to social manuevers, while most vampire mind control disciplines actually bypass the need for social manuevers (because mind control). That said? There's the Irraka Auspice benefit, and one Storm Lord merit relating to the social maneuvering, while the entire vinculum system in Vampire uses it, plus a new social style and a Carthian merit. In fact, that's the largest benefit of blood bonding someone - you always have a perfect impression with the target, letting you roll once a turn instead of days or weeks. Negotiating with a spirit in Werewolf uses social maneuvering, but then, its the same thing in Vampire with your fellow Kindred or, if your foolish enough, one of the strix. <br /> <br /> From a pure mechanical standpoint, it seems that they are roughly equal. In Vampire, it may seem like you need it less, again because mind control disciplines allow you to bypass the system, but I use it heavily for a ton of interactions in VtR, especially whenever they're trying to get something, like negotiating for temporary feeding rights, establishing a haven in someone else's backyard, gathering allies, throwing parties, convincing the Prince that no, you didn't break the Masquerde, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}